 "verses": {
  "bsb|GEN 14:18": {
   "text": "Then Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine—since he was priest of God Most High —"
  },
  "bsb|GEN 14:19": {
   "text": "and he blessed Abram and said: “Blessed be Abram by God Most High, Creator of heaven and earth,"
  },
  "bsb|GEN 14:20": {
   "text": "and blessed be God Most High, who has delivered your enemies into your hand.” Then Abram gave Melchizedek a tenth of everything."
  },
  "bsb|GEN 17:5": {
   "text": "No longer will you be called Abram, but your name will be Abraham, for I have made you a father of many nations."
  },
  "bsb|HEB 7:1": {
   "text": "This Melchizedek was king of Salem and priest of God Most High. He met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him,"
  },
  "bsb|HEB 7:10": {
   "text": "For when Melchizedek met Abraham, Levi was still in the loin of his ancestor."
  },
  "bsb|HEB 7:4": {
   "text": "Consider how great Melchizedek was: Even the patriarch Abraham gave him a tenth of the plunder."
  },
  "bsb|HEB 7:7": {
   "text": "And indisputably, the lesser is blessed by the greater."
  },
  "bsb|HEB 7:9": {
   "text": "And so to speak, Levi, who collects the tenth, paid the tenth through Abraham."
  },
